WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.529
You might still be in shock following the
ending of Avengers: Infinity War, but hope

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:06.620
is on the way in the form of Captain Marvel.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.200
It's worth wondering how any new superhero
can beat back Thanos after the Mad Titan took

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.160
down just about every other Avenger.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.400
We've combed through decades of comics and
months of interviews to find out just how

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.500
powerful Captain Marvel really is.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.720
From her energy absorption powers to her intergalactic
political prowess, here are the ways that

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.660
Captain Marvel could win the war against Thanos
in Avengers 4.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.000
Marvel-ous powers

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.960
In the comics, Captain Marvel is easily one
of the heaviest hitters in the Marvel Universe.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.520
During Infinity, one of the Thanos-centric
storylines that served as an inspiration for

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.969
Avengers: Infinity War, Carol Danvers is part
of the strike team of Avengers that attacks

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:45.880
Thanos and his Black Order on Earth.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.860
That team includes Hulk, Thor, and Hyperion,
who is basically Marvel's equivalent to Superman.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.460
That's a powerful group, and Captain Marvel
is as strong as any of them.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.100
"Carol Danvers, aka, Captain Marvel, aka my
favorite new Avenger."

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.190
Beyond her powers of super strength, flight,
and energy blasts, she also has the ability

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.120
to absorb various forms of energy.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.260
Like Chumbawumba, Captain Marvel gets knocked
down, but gets back up again.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.300
Thanos might be strong, but this will be the
first time onscreen that he'll be fighting

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.100
someone who gets stronger the more power he
throws at her.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:19.940
Binary

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:24.340
One of Carol Danvers' key attributes is her
status as a cosmic hero.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.840
No matter what team she's a part of, her adventures
very often take her to space.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:34.550
In Uncanny X-Men #163, Carol and the X-Men
were kidnapped by an alien race known as the

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.620
Brood, who performed experiments on her.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.620
Their genetic meddling unlocked a new level
of power for Danvers, giving her a new identity,

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.900
Binary, and a physical connection with the
connective tissue of the universe.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:49.960
Carol eventually burned out her new powers
after restoring a dying sun to full health

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:54.020
and returned to her previous power levels
— although when she overloads her absorption

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:57.560
powers, she's still able to tap into Binary
form temporarily.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.000
Thanos has no idea what he's in for.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.100
Cinematic smackdown

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.800
Of course, the powers we previously mentioned
are all from the comics.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.800
Even if she's powerful in the comics, she
can't possibly be more powerful than an Asgardian

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.700
god or the Sorcerer Supreme in the movies,
right?

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:14.640
Wrong.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:19.580
According to none other than Marvel Studios
chief Kevin Feige himself, Carol Danvers is

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.390
more formidable than anyone else we've seen
in the MCU thus far.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.500
In a talk with Vulture, Feige said:

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.160
"With Captain Marvel, she is as powerful a
character as we've ever put in a movie.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.810
Her powers are off the charts, and when she's
introduced, she will be by far the strongest

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.020
character we've ever had."

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.280
There's a very good chance that the cinematic
Carol Danvers can take down Thanos in a straight-up

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.240
fight, even without the help of the other
Avengers.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.600
Adapting Infinity Gauntlet

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:50.980
Infinity served as a major inspiration for
some scenes in Infinity War, like the Wakanda

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:54.980
invasion and Thanos' Black Order helping him
fight Earth's mightiest heroes.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.800
But it wasn't the biggest influence on the
film's plot.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:03.300
That honor goes to Infinity Gauntlet, a miniseries
that features Thanos assembling the Infinity

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:07.460
Gauntlet, destroying half of the universe
in a single snap, capturing and torturing

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:11.930
his daughter Nebula, and fighting various
Avengers with the power of his cosmically

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.020
powerful Gauntlet.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.160
Sound familiar?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.880
In Infinity Gauntlet, the remaining heroes
who fight Thanos are led by a being with cosmic

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.460
awareness named Adam Warlock.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:24.960
While Adam Warlock is due to appear in Guardians
of the Galaxy 3, it's been confirmed that

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.510
we won't see him in Avengers 4 — so it's
much more likely that directors Joe and Anthony

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.420
Russo will sub in Captain Marvel.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.400
Man with a plan

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.160
The reason that we're even talking about Captain
Marvel's involvement in the upcoming Avengers

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.380
flick is due to Nick Fury dialing her up on
a space pager at the end of Avengers: Infinity

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:43.880
War.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.200
Fury has faked his death at least once onscreen,
and the man's got a plan for everything.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.420
It's not unlikely that he's anticipated an
event on this scale, and worked out that plan

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.420
with Danvers before she left for space.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:59.300
While Fury might be gone in Avengers 4, the
massive network of SHIELD operatives should

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.060
still be around.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.620
Well, half of them, anyway.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.280
It makes sense that they would turn to the
woman that's most experienced to take advantage

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:05.780
of it.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.940
Military expertise

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.470
Aside from her powers, there's another aspect
to Captain Marvel that might come into play

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.900
for Avengers 4: her military experience and
role as a leader.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.950
She was an Executive Director of SHIELD in
the Ultimate Universe — and even in the

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.900
"regular" Marvel universe, she was a colonel
in the Air Force.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:27.600
Not to mention the many times she's led a
team of heroes for interplanetary defense

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.840
or as the head of Alpha Flight.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:34.010
While her superpowers and fighting prowess
are arguably the flashiest aspects of the

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.780
character, it might just be her military leadership
that helps her rally the Avengers to finally

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:39.800
stop Thanos.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.780
Thanks for watching!

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.460
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.680
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

